  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe optimization approach will remain as perturbed local optimization, but with improved exploration. The key improvements are:\n- Multiple initialization strategies to escape local minima\n- Enhanced perturbation with varying scales\n- Better handling of feasibility constraints\nThe strategy addresses the non-convex optimization challenge by employing multiple starting points and systematic perturbations, ensuring a more comprehensive search for the global minimum.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe represent h as a vector h[i] \u2208 [0,1] with \u2211h[i] = n_points/2. The objective is to minimize C5 = max_k (correlate(h, 1\u2212h,k)) * dx. The perturbation strategy uses multiple initial points and systematically explores the solution space.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialize with initial_h_values if available, else uniform\nb. Generate multiple perturbation patterns\nc. Optimize each perturbed starting point\nd. Track the best solution\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Use multiple perturbation scales\n- Try different optimization steps\n- Use varied initialization strategies\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nThe approach balances exploration and exploitation within the time budget, ensuring progress even if individual optimizations fail.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nThe solution ensures feasibility and validates the final candidate against the task metric.",
